{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789909635,"nonce":"wuI7k1wq6qMt9RplXJao6CjEyOo=","title":"Rest arguments: `...r:T` parsed as a plain parameter, spread rejected, `Rest\u003cT\u003e` methods untyped","message":"A function `f(...r:Int)` was lowered with `r:Int`, so `f(1,2,3)` was an\narity error and `r.length` / `r[0]` did not type. `f(...arr)` did not parse.\nOn `haxe.Rest\u003cString\u003e` the abstract's own type parameter was never\nregistered, so `toArray():Array\u003cT\u003e` came back as `Array\u003cT\u003e` unsubstituted\nand `rest.length` resolved by bare name to another class's `length`\n(`List.length`) in a large module set.\n\nFix, in one batch:\n- parser: `...name:Type` is `haxe.Rest\u003cType\u003e` (`Rest\u003cDynamic\u003e` when\n  unannotated) in both parsers and in function types; `...expr` in call\n  arguments is `ExprKind::Spread`.\n- tast: trailing arguments for a Rest formal are packed into one\n  `haxe.Rest\u003cT\u003e` array literal at the call site; a spread argument is passed\n  through. Abstract declarations register their type parameters like\n  classes; an `Array\u003cT\u003e` return substitutes the receiver's element\n  (`NeedArray`). A Class-kind typedef whose target is `Array` is typed as the\n  array.\n- mir: abstract property accessors and methods are exported to the\n  cross-module maps; a MIR-wrapper getter is a stdlib forward reference; a\n  Placeholder/Array/String receiver never carries a user field.\n\nConformance 573 -\u003e 577 (Issue10761, Issue10906, Issue13016, Issue2979);\nIssue10205/Issue10955/Issue6036 CRASH/COMPILE_FAIL -\u003e WRONG_ANSWER; TestRest\nCOMPILE_FAIL -\u003e CRASH (separate issue). Fixture\nhaxe-conformance/regressions/RestArgs.hx.","files":null}]}